1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Python is the most popular programming language in the world because of its simple and beginner-friendly syntax.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
And that's the number one reason it's hated by C++ programmers.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
It's the language of choice for artificial intelligence and machine learning,

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
but also heavily used in scripting, automation, and backend development.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
It has a huge ecosystem of third-party libraries such as Numpi for numerical computing, pandas,

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,960
for data analysis, psychic learn, for machine learning, tensor flow, for deep learning,

7
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:34,720
Django, for building web applications, and Keevy for cross-platform, desktop, and mobile apps.

8
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:40,560
In case you care, Python is 33 years old. It was created by a Dutch programmer in 1991

9
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:46,160
and named after the British comedy Monty Python. Python is an interpreted language, meaning you can

10
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:51,280
run your code without the compilation step. But you need an interpreter that's written in C for

11
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:56,800
performance. Unlike other languages, Python has hidden gems. We can import this for the

12
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:03,760
zen of Python or anti-gravity for a fun surprise. We can declare a variable with a name and a value

13
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:08,800
that can be a string, a Boolean, or a number. Python is a dynamically typed language,

14
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:13,920
meaning the type of variables is determined at runtime. Unlike other languages in Python,

15
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:19,600
we can add or even multiply strings and numbers. Python has four types of collections, lists,

16
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:26,000
topples, sets, and dictionaries. Now, unlike many languages, we can use a negative index to count

17
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:32,080
backwards. To define a function, we use the dev keyword and indentation to declare a block of code,

18
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:37,200
so no curly braces. And that's another reason Python is hated by C++ programmers.

19
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:42,240
Python also supports object-oriented programming. We can define classes using the class keyword and

20
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:47,840
have them inherit from each other. Python comes with batteries included, a huge library of built-in

21
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:54,720
modules for tasks like working with CSV, JSON, emails, web scraping, and so on. And that was Python

22
00:01:54,720 --> 00:02:04,240
in two minutes. Want to learn Python? Check out my tutorials.

